[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/786670875","html_url":"https://github.com/vuejs/core/issues/3315#issuecomment-786670875","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/3315","id":786670875,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc4NjY3MDg3NQ==","user":{"login":"edison1105","id":3705199,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUxOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3705199?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105","html_url":"https://github.com/edison1105","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-02-26T14:12:03Z","updated_at":"2021-02-26T15:21:11Z","body":"It's not a bug.this is intentional in options api.\r\n\r\nyou will see your expected use `setup`:\r\n```javascript\r\n  setup(){\r\n    const arr = [1, 2, 3].map((num) => ({ num: ref(num) }))\r\n    arr.forEach((el) => {\r\n      console.log(el.num);\r\n      console.log(el.num.value);\r\n    });\r\n  }\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/786670875/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"edison1105","id":3705199,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUxOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3705199?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105","html_url":"https://github.com/edison1105","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edison1105/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/786726271","html_url":"https://github.com/vuejs/core/issues/3315#issuecomment-786726271","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/3315","id":786726271,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc4NjcyNjI3MQ==","user":{"login":"shameleo","id":11148445,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTQ4NDQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11148445?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shameleo","html_url":"https://github.com/shameleo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shameleo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shameleo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shameleo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shameleo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shameleo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shameleo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shameleo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shameleo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shameleo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-02-26T15:45:51Z","updated_at":"2021-02-26T16:13:29Z","body":"If it is true than I have a lot of questions:\r\n1) Using refs is forbidden in optional API? I didn't see any docs or runtime warnings about it.\r\n2) Huge amount of tricks would be not available in optional API. Refs bound to URL params, local storage or many other use cases when some factory function returns ref or computed ref. For example, I noticed the issue, when I tried to make tree node, with `checked` prop as ref, which is updated when children's corresponding `checked` props updated. I can't do it? A HUGE dissapointment.\r\n3) Some libs will only can be used with composition API ([for instance](https://github.com/MartinMalinda/vue-concurrency)). And it is problem as we can't use data and methods from options API in `setup`, so whole component must be written in composition style.\r\n4) As a result, options API is second class citizen now, and it's not even matter of choice.\r\n\r\nIf 1-4 is not true, and it's actually works than why typescript should tell me it doesn't?\r\n\r\nPS. More appropriate example of composition API would be\r\n```js\r\nimport { defineComponent, ref, reactive } from \"vue\";\r\n\r\nexport default defineComponent({\r\n  setup() {\r\n    const r = reactive({\r\n      arr: [1, 2, 3].map((num) => ({ num: ref(num) }))\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    r.arr.forEach(el => { console.log(el.num) });\r\n  }\r\n});\r\n```\r\nIt all about unwrapping.\r\n\r\nPS2. Example is a bit overcomplicated (array of objects instead of simple ref) because I couldn't reproduce issue with just ref. I can now, and it's confusing. Don't know if either different IDE or different packages or whatever made the difference.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/786726271/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1"